course: dictionary
lesson: 10124
title: Thoughtful: kind or deep in thought
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thoughtful has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. «Thank you, it was so thoughtful of you» means someone thought about your feelings and did something kind. Here thoughtful means kind and considerate.
explain: «Others are hard, and thoughtful people disagree» is about people who think carefully and seriously. Here thoughtful means thinking quietly and seriously about a question. Try swapping in careful or serious and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Thoughtful can also describe work. A thoughtful answer shows careful thinking. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a person, a way of thinking, or a piece of work. The clues will show you which meaning fits.
fact: Thoughtful means thinking about what other people need or feel, and being kind to them.
fact: Thoughtful can also mean thinking quietly and seriously about something.
fact: «A thoughtful gift» or «a thoughtful answer» shows care or careful thinking.
fact: «How thoughtful of you» is a polite way to thank someone for a kind act.
fact: Thoughtful is an adjective, and it changes to more thoughtful and most thoughtful.
exercise: «Thank you, it was so thoughtful of you.» What does thoughtful mean here? | Old and worn out | Very loud | *Kind, because someone thought about your feelings | Careless and rushed
exercise: «Others are hard, and thoughtful people disagree.» What does thoughtful mean here? | *Thinking quietly and seriously | Silly and noisy | Late for school | Happy and excited
exercise: A teacher praises «a thoughtful answer». What does this suggest? | The answer was wrong | *The answer shows careful thinking | The answer was very short | The answer was copied from a book
test: Ruby remembered her friend's birthday and made her a card. Which word describes Ruby? | Lazy | Noisy | Angry | *Thoughtful
test: Sam sat still, chin in hand, thinking hard about the puzzle. Which word describes Sam? | *Thoughtful | Excited | Bored | Hungry
exam: Which sentence uses thoughtful to mean thinking quietly and seriously? | The bus was thoughtful and late | The cake was thoughtful and warm | *Mia sat in a thoughtful silence, weighing up both sides | The gift was thoughtful and sweet
